\ TINYREF — FreeForth2 Core Quick Reference (x86 + x86-64)
\
\ Core words only. See QUICKREF for full list (libs, OS, FPU, etc).
\ One line per word: name, stack effect, short description.
\ Derived from ff.help (x86) and ff64.help (x86-64 additions).
\
\ Notation:
\   n=number  @=address  #=count  c=char/byte  ?=boolean
\   xx=double-cell (PNO accumulator)  f:x=FP stack item
\   ( == ) = return stack effect
\   Backtick words (e.g. dup`) are compile-time macros.
\   Without the backtick: inline at compile time. With it: call at runtime.
\   [x86-64]    = x86-64 only or differs from x86
\   [x86 only]  = x86 only, not present on x86-64
\
\ FLAGS annotations (verified empirically on both platforms):
\   [F:ZCSO] = sets Zero, Carry, Sign, Overflow flags (SUB, ADD, CMP)
\   [F:ZS]   = sets Zero and Sign; clears Carry (AND, OR, XOR)
\   [F:ZSO]  = sets Zero, Sign, Overflow; CF unchanged (INC, DEC)
\   [F:ZF]   = sets/returns Zero flag (comparators like within, find)
\   [F:--]   = flags undefined after this word (MUL, DIV)
\   No annotation = flags-preserving (MOV/LEA/PUSH/POP don't touch FLAGS)
\
\ Jcc selector annotations (which flag the selector reads):
\   [ZF] [SF] [CF] [ZF+SF]
\
\ FLAGS-based conditionals: comparisons set CPU flags, NOT booleans.
\ 0=/0<>/0</0> store a Jcc opcode — NO runtime code emitted.

