\ =============== CONCEPTS ==================================
\ DATAstack  — separate data stack; TOS cached in registers
\ CALLstack  — return stack; also loop counters, >r temps
\ TOS        — top of stack (rightmost in diagrams)
\ NOS        — next of stack (second element)
\ SWAPbit    — SC bit1: which register is TOS vs NOS
\ CALLbit    — SC bit0: data/call stack pointer swap [x86 only]
\ anonymous  — unnamed defs auto-execute on ; (STATE-free)
\ backquote  — ` suffix marks macros (immediate execution)
\ FLAGS      — CPU flags drive conditionals (not booleans)
